## Problem

The Cursor gRPC proxy (vendored from opencode-cursor-oauth) hangs indefinitely when OpenAI-compatible requests include `tools` definitions. Non-tool requests work fine (3-4s response time).

## Root cause hypothesis

The proxy translates OpenAI tool definitions to Cursor's MCP tool protobuf format via `buildMcpToolDefinitions()`, but the response handling for tool call results appears to be incomplete. When Cursor returns a tool call response, the proxy's streaming handler may not properly detect the end of the response or may be waiting for a tool result that never comes.

## Reproduction

```javascript
// This hangs:
fetch('http://127.0.0.1:32123/v1/chat/completions', {
  method: 'POST',
  body: JSON.stringify({
    model: 'composer-2',
    messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Use the calculator' }],
    tools: [{ type: 'function', function: { name: 'calc', ... } }],
  }),
});

// This works fine:
fetch('http://127.0.0.1:32123/v1/chat/completions', {
  method: 'POST',
  body: JSON.stringify({
    model: 'composer-2',
    messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello' }],
  }),
});
```

## Impact

- Composer 2 works for text-only interactions in OpenCode
- Tool calling (Bash, Read, Write, etc.) does not work — requests hang
- This means Composer 2 is currently limited to conversational use, not coding tasks

## Investigation needed

- Check `proxy.js` streaming handler for tool call response parsing
- Compare with Nomadcxx/opencode-cursor's tool handling (they have a full tool execution chain)
- The vendored proxy may need the tool loop from the Nomadcxx plugin to properly handle Cursor's MCP tool protocol

## Related

- t1551 (GH#5446) — original Cursor proxy implementation
- Nomadcxx/opencode-cursor — has working tool execution (cursor-agent CLI approach)
